3.0's ghost code either has a bug or a vastly unfair advantage.
I took a level 4 or 5 tourist (okay, I'm being bloody-minded about
making a tourist a playable character) down to a bones level and
met a ghost.  I tried to fight him for a while, but couldn't get
anywhere.  Down to 1 hp with no hope left, I decided to convert
the game to explore mode.  I eventually got backed into a corridor
with an immovable boulder on one side, the ghost on the other.
I pounded on that sucker as hard as I could (with an orcish dagger,
I think) and *never* hit it.  I kept at it for maybe 20 deaths,
about 1000 moves perhaps, and *never* hit the ghost.  I can believe
ghosts being tough, but invulnerable?  Shouldn't even weak characters
have *some* chance, however slim, of hitting tough-AC opponents?

Luckily I had a wand of make invisible with me...

